  "final_output": "# Deployment Rollback Procedure\n\n## Stop condition\n\n**Stop the rollback immediately if the service error rate exceeds 2% at any stage.**\n\nIf triggered:\n\n1. Pause all rollback and traffic changes.\n2. Keep traffic in its current safe state; do not continue shifting traffic.\n3. Notify the incident commander or escalation contact.\n4. Preserve logs, metrics, and deployment events for investigation.\n\n## Procedure\n\n1. **Confirm the rollback target**\n   - Identify the last known-good application version.\n   - Confirm that the database migration is backward-compatible.\n   - **Do not roll back the database migration.**\n\n2. **Start monitoring**\n   - Open dashboards for error rate, request volume, latency, and instance health.\n   - Confirm that the error-rate alert threshold is set to **greater than 2%**.\n   - Record the current application version and key metrics.\n\n3. **Drain traffic**\n   - Remove the deployment from load-balancer or ingress rotation.\n   - Wait until active connections and in-flight requests have completed.\n   - Verify that no new production traffic is reaching the deployment.\n   - **Do not begin the application rollback until traffic is fully drained.**\n\n4. **Roll back the application**\n   - Deploy the last known-good application version.\n   - Leave the backward-compatible database migration in place.\n   - Verify that all rolled-back instances start successfully and pass readiness and health checks.\n   - If the error rate exceeds 2%, apply the stop condition.\n\n5. **Restore traffic gradually**\n   - Return a small portion of traffic to the rolled-back deployment.\n   - Monitor error rate, latency, and instance health.\n   - Increase traffic in controlled steps only while the error rate remains at or below 2%.\n   - If the error rate exceeds 2%, stop further traffic changes and apply the stop condition.\n\n6. **Complete and verify**\n   - Restore normal traffic only after the rolled-back version remains healthy.\n   - Confirm that the expected application version is running on all instances.\n   - Continue monitoring until the service is stable.\n   - Document the rollback time, versions, observed metrics, and any errors.",
